1
00:00:00,563 --> 00:00:07,921
Welcome to GodrejWMS. This short video shows
how Putaway Preferences work.

2
00:00:08,326 --> 00:00:12,060
You maintain Brand and AOP masters.

3
00:00:12,464 --> 00:00:17,062
Then you map each brand to a preferred range
of locations.

4
00:00:17,467 --> 00:00:23,313
The system uses that range to suggest putaway
locations for incoming stock.

5
00:00:25,077 --> 00:00:29,123
Open Brand Master from the Master Data menu.

6
00:00:29,530 --> 00:00:34,560
This screen holds the brand codes used by the
Material Master.

7
00:00:34,963 --> 00:00:37,257
Click New Brand.

8
00:00:37,660 --> 00:00:44,394
Brand Code is mandatory. Enter “Stella”.

9
00:00:44,796 --> 00:00:47,762
Add a description if you like.

10
00:00:48,164 --> 00:00:50,842
Then click Save Brand.

11
00:00:51,243 --> 00:00:56,489
The new brand appears in the list as Active.

12
00:00:58,251 --> 00:01:02,993
Search for the brand by code or description.

13
00:01:03,396 --> 00:01:07,034
Click the pencil icon on its row.

14
00:01:07,438 --> 00:01:10,092
Change the description.

15
00:01:10,493 --> 00:01:17,779
Untick Active to make a brand inactive, so it
is no longer offered for materials.

16
00:01:18,182 --> 00:01:20,572
Click Save Brand.

17
00:01:20,973 --> 00:01:24,827
The grid shows the updated description.

18
00:01:26,588 --> 00:01:30,370
Next, AOP Description Master.

19
00:01:30,771 --> 00:01:35,513
It stores the AOP codes used by the Material
Master.

20
00:01:35,916 --> 00:01:38,858
Click New AOP Code.

21
00:01:39,260 --> 00:01:43,426
AOP Code is mandatory. Enter “Stella”.

22
00:01:43,828 --> 00:01:46,410
Add its description.

23
00:01:46,812 --> 00:01:49,802
Click Save AOP Code.

24
00:01:50,204 --> 00:01:53,962
The new code appears in the list as Active.

25
00:01:55,722 --> 00:02:00,824
Updating works the same way. Search for the
code.

26
00:02:01,225 --> 00:02:05,511
Click the pencil icon and change the
description.

27
00:02:05,913 --> 00:02:15,023
Use Active to retire a code. Inactive codes
are not offered for materials.

28
00:02:15,424 --> 00:02:18,414
Click Save AOP Code.

29
00:02:18,816 --> 00:02:22,406
The list shows the updated description.

30
00:02:24,162 --> 00:02:29,480
Now the key step. Open Brand Location
Preferences.

31
00:02:29,884 --> 00:02:34,146
At the moment, no brand has a preferred range.

32
00:02:34,549 --> 00:02:36,963
Click New Mapping.

33
00:02:37,363 --> 00:02:42,081
Choose the Brand Code: Cinthol.

34
00:02:42,483 --> 00:02:48,113
Choose the Warehouse (GCPL) and the Rack (B1).

35
00:02:48,514 --> 00:02:54,888
Location Preference From: B-11-01.

36
00:02:55,290 --> 00:02:59,552
Location Preference To: B-12-03.

37
00:02:59,966 --> 00:03:06,652
The range covers columns 11–12 and levels 1–3
of rack B1.

38
00:03:07,053 --> 00:03:09,491
Click Save Mapping.

39
00:03:09,893 --> 00:03:15,739
The mapping appears with its warehouse, rack
and location range.

40
00:03:16,141 --> 00:03:25,011
Pencil = edit a mapping. Bin = remove it. A
brand can have more than one mapping.

41
00:03:26,772 --> 00:03:34,346
First, here is what happens without a mapping.

42
00:03:34,750 --> 00:03:41,484
Receive 100 boxes of a Cinthol material and
100 boxes of a GK material.

43
00:03:46,085 --> 00:03:52,483
Submit Inward. The Allocation Result shows the
suggested locations.

44
00:03:52,888 --> 00:04:00,438
With no mapping, both materials go to rack A,
starting at A-01-01.

45
00:04:02,198 --> 00:04:07,468
The same receipt again, after saving the
Cinthol mapping.

46
00:04:16,222 --> 00:04:24,420
Cinthol is now suggested inside the mapped
range: B-11-01 and B-11-02.

47
00:04:24,826 --> 00:04:32,328
GK has no mapping, so standard logic applies.
It stays in rack A.

48
00:04:32,730 --> 00:04:44,888
Rule order: inside the brand range — top up the same SKU, then consolidate, then best
empty location.

49
00:04:45,293 --> 00:04:54,259
Only if quantity remains does it look outside the range. A strong preference, not a hard
block.

50
00:04:56,028 --> 00:05:02,210
Keep your Brand and AOP masters clean and up
to date.

51
00:05:02,615 --> 00:05:08,221
Update mappings when you add new brands, racks
or locations.

52
00:05:08,626 --> 00:05:14,736
Check capacity — a range that is too small
pushes stock outside it.

53
00:05:15,142 --> 00:05:17,700
Thank you for watching.
